# CODEOWNERS puts a named person on changes whose blast radius is every repo that installs this
# marketplace. The main-branch ruleset requires both an approving review and a CODEOWNER review;
# because the wildcard below covers every path, no pull request can merge on automation alone.
# `Validate marketplace` is the sole required status check and handles deterministic correctness.
#
# This repo ships no application code, so the product-shaped paths in the shared asset
# (plugins/plenipo/skills/setup/assets/CODEOWNERS — /src/**/Authorization/ and friends) do not exist
# here. The spine is instead the machinery that decides whether a skill is fit to publish.

* @abrahamFerga

# The verifier. An agent that can edit its own checks has no checks.
/eng/                      @abrahamFerga

# The manifests. A bad one breaks installation for every repo downstream, not just this one.
/.claude-plugin/           @abrahamFerga
/plugins/*/.claude-plugin/ @abrahamFerga

# The contract the validator enforces, and the "do not contradict these" fact list.
/AUTHORING.md              @abrahamFerga
/AGENTS.md                 @abrahamFerga

# The harness itself. An agent that can edit its own gates has no gates.
/.github/                  @abrahamFerga
/CODEOWNERS                @abrahamFerga
/workflow.json             @abrahamFerga
